      "problem": "Evaluate the indicator function\n$1[3\\in \\{1,3,6,8\\}].$",
      "worked_solution": "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the predicate is $3\\in \\{1,3,6,8\\}.$ Since $3$ is an element of the set $\\{1,3,6,8\\},$ the predicate is true. Therefore,\n\n$$\n1[3\\in \\{1,3,6,8\\}]=1.\n$$",
